/* B.E. F.A.S.T. */
"Stroke symptoms come on suddenly. If you notice any one of these signs, call 911 or your local emergency number immediately. Fast treatment can save brain function." = "中風症狀來得很突然。只要發現其中任何一個徵兆，請立即撥打 911 或當地緊急電話（台灣為 119）。及早治療能保住大腦功能。";
"Sudden loss of balance or coordination, dizziness, or trouble walking." = "突然失去平衡或協調、頭暈或行走困難。";
"Sudden blurred or double vision, or loss of vision in one or both eyes." = "突然視線模糊或複視，或一眼或雙眼看不見。";
"One side of the face droops or feels numb. The smile may look uneven." = "一側臉部下垂或發麻，笑容可能不對稱。";
"Sudden weakness or numbness in an arm or leg, often on one side of the body." = "手臂或腿突然無力或麻木，通常在身體一側。";
"Slurred speech, trouble speaking or understanding, or sudden confusion." = "說話含糊、說話或理解困難，或突然意識混亂。";
"Call 911 right away, even if the symptoms go away. Note the time they started." = "即使症狀消失，也要立即撥打 911 或當地緊急電話（台灣為 119）。記下症狀開始的時間。";

/* Types of stroke */
"Types of stroke" = "中風類型";
"Strokes are caused either by a blockage or by bleeding. A TIA is a temporary warning." = "中風是由血管阻塞或出血造成。TIA 是暫時性的警訊。";
"Ischemic stroke" = "缺血性中風";
"The most common type, about 87% of strokes." = "最常見的類型，約占中風的 87%。";
"An ischemic stroke happens when a blood clot or narrowed artery blocks blood flow to part of the brain." = "當血栓或狹窄的動脈阻斷流向部分大腦的血液時，就會發生缺血性中風。";
"Clot-dissolving medicine works best when given within a few hours of the first symptoms." = "血栓溶解劑在症狀出現後數小時內使用效果最好。";
"Doctors may also remove large clots with a catheter (thrombectomy)." = "醫師也可以用導管取出較大的血栓（取栓術）。";
"Every minute counts, so call 911 or your local emergency number right away." = "分秒必爭，請立即撥打 911 或當地緊急電話（台灣為 119）。";
"Hemorrhagic stroke" = "出血性中風";
"Less common, about 13% of strokes, but often more severe." = "較少見，約占中風的 13%，但通常更嚴重。";
"A hemorrhagic stroke happens when a weakened blood vessel breaks and bleeds into or around the brain, raising pressure and damaging tissue." = "當脆弱的血管破裂，血液流入腦內或腦周圍時，就會發生出血性中風，使腦壓升高並損傷組織。";
"High blood pressure is a common cause." = "高血壓是常見原因。";
"Treatment may include lowering blood pressure and surgery to stop the bleeding or relieve pressure." = "治療可能包括降血壓，以及以手術止血或減輕壓力。";
"Aneurysms can be clipped or coiled to seal the vessel." = "動脈瘤可以用夾閉或線圈栓塞來封住血管。";
"Transient ischemic attack" = "暫時性腦缺血發作";
"A \"mini-stroke\" with symptoms that go away." = "症狀會消失的「小中風」。";
"A TIA is a brief blockage of blood flow to the brain. Its symptoms are the same as a stroke but usually last only minutes." = "TIA 是流向大腦的血液短暫受阻。症狀與中風相同，但通常只持續幾分鐘。";
"A TIA is a warning sign that a stroke may follow." = "TIA 是警訊，之後可能發生中風。";
"It needs emergency care, even if the symptoms are gone." = "即使症狀已經消失，仍需要緊急就醫。";
"Treating the cause can prevent a future stroke." = "治療病因可以預防日後中風。";

/* Risk factors */
"Risk factors" = "危險因子";
"Some conditions and habits make a stroke more likely. Many of them can be treated or changed." = "某些疾病和習慣會提高中風機率。其中許多可以治療或改變。";
"High blood pressure" = "高血壓";
"The leading cause of stroke. Over time it damages and weakens blood vessels." = "中風的首要原因。長期下來會損傷並削弱血管。";
"Diabetes" = "糖尿病";
"High blood sugar damages blood vessels and makes clots more likely." = "高血糖會損傷血管，並使血栓更容易形成。";
"Heart disease" = "心臟病";
"Conditions such as atrial fibrillation (AFib) can cause clots that travel to the brain." = "心房顫動等疾病可能形成血栓，並隨血流進入大腦。";
"Smoking" = "吸菸";
"Damages blood vessels and raises blood pressure." = "損傷血管並使血壓升高。";
"Sleep apnea" = "睡眠呼吸中止症";
"Repeated pauses in breathing during sleep strain the heart and blood vessels." = "睡眠中反覆呼吸中止，會加重心臟和血管的負擔。";
"Drug use" = "使用毒品";
"Drugs such as cocaine and amphetamines can trigger a stroke, even in young people." = "古柯鹼和安非他命等毒品可能引發中風，年輕人也不例外。";

/* Prevention */
"Lower your risk" = "降低風險";
"Most strokes are linked to risk factors you can manage. These habits help at any age." = "大多數中風與你能控制的危險因子有關。這些習慣在任何年齡都有幫助。";
"Control blood pressure" = "控制血壓";
"Check it regularly and take medicine as prescribed." = "定期量血壓，並遵照醫囑服藥。";
"Manage blood sugar" = "控制血糖";
"Keep diabetes under control with your care team." = "與醫療團隊一起控制好糖尿病。";
"Manage cholesterol" = "控制膽固醇";
"Ask your doctor how often to get it checked." = "問問醫師多久檢查一次。";
"Quit smoking and tobacco" = "戒菸";
"Your risk starts dropping soon after you quit." = "戒菸後不久，風險就開始下降。";
"Stay active" = "保持活動";
"Aim for about 30 minutes of moderate activity most days." = "大多數日子進行約 30 分鐘中等強度活動。";
"Eat a heart-healthy diet" = "吃得健康護心";
"More vegetables, fruit and whole grains; less salt and processed food." = "多吃蔬菜、水果和全穀類；少鹽、少加工食品。";
"Keep a healthy weight" = "維持健康體重";
"Even modest weight loss can lower blood pressure." = "即使只減一點體重，也能降低血壓。";
"Sleep well" = "睡個好覺";
"Aim for 7 to 9 hours, and get checked if you snore heavily." = "每晚睡 7 到 9 小時；如果打鼾很嚴重，請就醫檢查。";

/* Treatments */
"Treatment depends on the type of stroke and how quickly it begins. The sooner, the better." = "治療方式取決於中風類型和開始治療的速度。越早越好。";
"Clot-dissolving medicine" = "血栓溶解劑";
"Medicine given through an IV to break up a clot." = "經由靜脈注射、用來溶解血栓的藥物。";
"For ischemic stroke, a clot-dissolving medicine such as tPA can restore blood flow to the brain." = "對於缺血性中風，tPA 等血栓溶解劑可以恢復大腦的血流。";
"Works best when started within 3 to 4.5 hours of the first symptoms." = "在症狀出現後 3 到 4.5 小時內開始使用效果最好。";
"Can improve recovery and reduce disability." = "能改善復原並減少失能。";
"Not used when there is a high risk of bleeding, such as after recent surgery." = "出血風險高時（例如近期動過手術）不會使用。";
"Mechanical thrombectomy" = "機械取栓術";
"A catheter procedure to remove a large clot." = "以導管取出大型血栓的手術。";
"A thin tube is guided through an artery to the brain, where doctors remove the clot directly." = "醫師將細管沿著動脈送到大腦，直接取出血栓。";
"Can be done up to 24 hours after symptoms start for some patients." = "部分病人在症狀出現後 24 小時內仍可進行。";
"Often used together with clot-dissolving medicine for strokes in large arteries." = "大動脈中風時，常與血栓溶解劑合併使用。";
"Restores blood flow quickly to limit brain damage." = "迅速恢復血流，減少腦部損傷。";
"Surgery for bleeding" = "出血手術";
"Procedures to stop bleeding and relieve pressure." = "用於止血和減輕壓力的手術。";
"In a hemorrhagic stroke, surgery may be needed to stop the bleeding and lower pressure on the brain." = "出血性中風可能需要手術止血，並降低對大腦的壓力。";
"An aneurysm can be clipped or coiled to seal the bleeding vessel." = "動脈瘤可以用夾閉或線圈栓塞來封住出血的血管。";
"A craniotomy can remove pooled blood and relieve pressure." = "開顱手術可以清除積血並減輕壓力。";
"Quick treatment helps prevent further brain injury." = "及早治療有助於避免大腦進一步受損。";
"Rehabilitation" = "復健";
"Therapy to regain skills after a stroke." = "中風後幫助恢復能力的治療。";
"Recovery often continues for months. Rehabilitation helps people relearn movement, speech and everyday tasks." = "復原通常會持續數個月。復健能幫助病人重新學習活動、說話和日常事務。";
"May include physical, occupational and speech therapy." = "可能包括物理治療、職能治療和語言治療。";
"Starting early, while still in the hospital, tends to help." = "及早開始，住院期間就開始，通常更有幫助。";
"Family and caregivers are an important part of recovery." = "家人和照顧者是復原的重要一環。";

